#!/usr/bin/env python3
# tools/tf2-gate -- the Stage 4.2 headless scripted round gate.
#
# A python driver over tools/debug-api, built on tools/live-gate's own
# launch and read helpers (loaded by path from this file's own location):
# server_launch / client_launch / launch_with_free_port / Api and Game.kill.
#
# It boots a `-mod tf2` listen server (player 1, its own local client) plus a
# second headless client (player 2) that joins it -- the shape
# pair-boot.py boots -- and runs the plan's steps
# (docs/plans/tf2/stage4_milestone.md "Phase 4.2"):
#
#   1  join        both players present; the join asserted before any read
#   2  teams        mp_teams_unbalance_limit's default; jointeam auto on each
#                  puts them on different teams (2 and 3)
#   3  classes      joinclass scout / heavyweapons; max health 125 / 300;
#                  a +forward for 2 s measured from positions within 5 % of
#                  400 / 230
#   4  combat       the heavy fires at the scout at 200 u; the scout's
#                  Health drops (the stimulus must be non-zero)
#   5  heal         the joiner becomes a medic, the listen host becomes the
#                  heavy, is hurt first with the cheat command hurtme, and
#                  the medic heals him: Health rises, overheal to 450
#   6  ctf          scout carries the enemy flag home (score 1, flag home);
#                  forced tf2_dev_win yields TEAM_WIN -> RESTART -> PREROUND
#   7  changelevel  pl_badwater: the second map load; both games re-paint
#                  (the [SourceSharp/Hud] stamp is per level); the TF2 class
#                  census equals the counts recorded from the bsp's entity lump
#   8  payload      the BLU host pushes the func_tracktrain toward checkpoint
#                  1 (the cart moves only while he stands in the capper
#                  volume parented to it), the cart recedes once he is 500 u
#                  away, and riding it past the checkpoint node hands the
#                  team_control_point to BLU (path_track OnPass -> SetOwner;
#                  the owner outputs are read on the entity event ring)
#   9  mode switch  sv_mode null warms up (the [SourceSharp/Modes] needles,
#                  the 5 s sv_mode_switch_warmup), the round reaches PREROUND
#                  under it, sv_mode pl starts the round again, and the bare
#                  command answers active: 'pl'
#   10 teardown    both games exit; the server's /proc/<pid>/task count is
#                  recorded after the join and before the exit
#
# A listen server plus one joining client is used instead of a dedicated
# server plus two clients: tools/live-gate has no dedicated-server launch
# helper (server_launch IS the listen server -- maxplayers 4, a local
# client, +map), and the listen server's own local client is player 1, so
# listen server + joiner is the two-player game the steps need.
#
# Each step records its numbers to tools/.tf2-gate/<run>/report.tsv with
# TIP=$(git rev-parse HEAD) and its exit code, written as the step ends (a
# later crash cannot rewrite an earlier verdict). A step that cannot measure
# is a FAILURE, never a skip: a missing input (socket, paint line, field,
# /proc row) fails the gate.
#
# `--self-test` exercises the report writing and the pass/fail arithmetic
# without a game; tools/checks.tsv runs it as a routine check.
#
# NOT part of `make test`: it is a live gate. `make tf2-gate` runs it.
